    {
      "id": "pronunciation::steps.19.prompt",
      "path": "pronunciation/steps[19]/prompt",
      "ko": null,
      "en": "Liaison (연음화) occurs when a batchim is followed by a syllable that begins with…",
      "value": "연음화（連音化）發生在收音後面跟著以…開頭的音節時"
    },
    {
      "id": "pronunciation::steps.62.tip.text",
      "path": "pronunciation/steps[62]/tip.text",
      "ko": null,
      "en": "The palatalised ㅅ ('sh' sound) occurs before i-class vowels: 이 (i), 야 (ya), 여 (yeo), 요 (yo), 유 (yu). Before all other vowels — 아, 어, 오, 우, 으, and their compounds — ㅅ stays as a plain s sound. 사 is 'sa', but 시 is 'shi'.",
      "value": "口蓋化的ㅅ（sh音）在i類母音前出現：이（i）、야（ya）、여（yeo）、요（yo）、유（yu）。在所有其他母音——아、어、오、우、으及其複合——之前，ㅅ保持普通的s音。사是「sa」，但시是「shi」。"
    },
    {
      "id": "pronunciation::steps.45.body",
      "path": "pronunciation/steps[45]/body",
      "ko": null,
      "en": "When the consonants ㄷ or ㅌ appear as batchim and are followed by the vowel 이 (i), they shift forward in the mouth and change into ㅈ and ㅊ respectively. This shift is called palatalization — the consonant moves from the tooth ridge to the palate to anticipate the front vowel 이.",
      "value": "當子音ㄷ或ㅌ作為收音出現，後面跟著母音이（i）時，它們在口腔中前移，分別變成ㅈ和ㅊ。這種轉換稱為口蓋音化——子音從齒槽移動到上顎，以準備前元音이。"
    },
